  "question": {
    "text": "Geraniol, a volatile organic compound, is a component of rose oil. The density of the vapour is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>46</mn><msup><mi>gL</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>257</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mmHg</mi></math>. The molar mass of geraniol is (Nearest Integer)<br />[Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>082</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> atm <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>]"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "152",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Assuming ideal behaviour&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>dRT</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>760</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>257</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>273</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>530</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>46</mn><mi>gm</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math></p><p>So&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>46</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>082</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>530</mn></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>760</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>151</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>93</mn><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>152</mn></math></p>"
